url: "https://github.com/obedebessa/governance-drift"
abstract: >
  Manuscript source, closed-world detector study, separately implemented
  no-join baseline, canonical results, and bounded Kubernetes/GitOps
  laboratories measuring divergence between operational reality and the basis
  under which infrastructure was approved. The version 1.6.0 candidate adds
  activation-safe selection, temporal cuts, ablation, transition controls,
  real-process trace auditing, transport faults, live multi-deployment
  evaluation, and a bounded Argo CD/Gatekeeper cross-stack replication. Live
  outputs are provisional class-set classifications under the laboratory
  snapshot assumption; the completed cross-stack campaign reports 15/15 exact
  projected singleton classifications over declared evaluated components.
  Only configuration and policy use native second-stack surfaces;
  authorization reuses the shared adapter, and intent/environment are not
  evaluated there.
keywords:
  - "governance drift"
  - "configuration drift"
  - "GitOps"
  - "cloud governance"
  - "reproducibility"
